  "obstruction": "While there are three structurally similar facts (F:ml430-int-add-modeq-right-e58108ee for the commuted Int version, and F:ml430-nat-add-modeq-left-e3b1fba9 and F:ml430-nat-add-modeq-right-e2f11f21 for Nat versions), they are in different type domains (Int vs Nat) with different modEq predicates (ZMOD vs MOD). The Int.add_modEq_right sibling differs only by commutativity of addition, making it the sole Int-domain sibling. A general route would require at least three Int facts with the same n+a\u2261a pattern, but only two exist in the eligible set.",
